From 827d2b158cb556d8b6e5b94473c0541388d4e5ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:11:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(intro): Your first read, the onboarding tutorial in the
 Today hero slot; JS 0.9.2

A fresh install (and every existing install, once) meets a Start here card
where the resume hero normally sits. Tapping it opens the reader on a
bundled tutorial text that plays by itself: it starts at 200 words per
minute, ramps to 300 over about thirty seconds, and the copy is about
exactly that (you started at 200, you are now at 300, faster than the
average adult). Then the controls tuck themselves away on cue, the speed
pill unlocks, and the text teaches the gestures before sending the reader
to the shelf.

- src/intro.ts: the script as four beats with a per-word speed curve
  (word space, not wall-clock, so pausing or scrubbing cannot desync the
  copy), tokenized with parseText's own rule.
- The ramp rides the engine's existing pacingOverride (the narration
  mechanism): no change to the reel engine's frame worklet.
- ReaderScreen: the intro always runs in the Focus view (no mode
  selector) without touching the saved mode; auto-plays one beat after
  mount (waiting out a finger on the reel); chrome stays pinned until the
  handoff word, then normal auto-hide; after the handoff the pill drives
  a local stepper value, so the reader's own WPM setting is never
  written; no progress row, no session stats; marks the intro seen.
- ReaderChrome: the WPM pill's readout reads the scripted speed
  (subscribing to the index on its own, like ChapterProgress) with the
  stepper dimmed and inert while the script is in force.
- Store: persisted introSeen, schema v7 (older installs see the card once).
- Settings: Replay the intro. Today: Skip.
- scripts/test-intro.mjs, chained from test-tokenize.mjs so npm test
  covers it without touching package.json (its scripts block is an Expo
  fingerprint input; the fingerprint is verified unchanged from master):
  token-space equivalence, no chapter detection, the curve and its
  handoff, ramp timing (25-40 s), and the one-word display rules.

